<title>USA: No cold threat to Brazil coffee this weekend - WSC.</title>
<headline>No cold threat to Brazil coffee this weekend - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>No major cold is in sight in Brazil's coffee growing areas in the next three to five days, forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>Temperatures are forecast near normal on Friday and above normal on Saturday and through to Tuesday.</p>
<p>Conditions are generally favourable for the trees but some disruptions to the harvest are still expected from scattered showers.</p>
</text>
